

This method reverses the digits of a 32‑bit signed integer. It extracts digits one by one, builds the reversed number, and checks for overflow or underflow before each update. If reversing causes the value to exceed integer limits, it returns 0; otherwise, it returns the reversed number.

Complexity analysis:
Time Complexity: O(d)
where d is the number of digits in x (at most 10 for a 32‑bit integer).
Space Complexity: O(1)
uses constant extra space.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public int reverse(int x) {
        int rev=0;
        while(x!=0){
            int digit=x%10;
            x/=10;
            if(rev>Integer.MAX_VALUE/10 || (rev== Integer.MAX_VALUE/10 && digit>7)){
                return 0;
            }
            if(rev<Integer.MIN_VALUE /10|| (rev== Integer.MIN_VALUE/10 && digit<-8)){
                return 0;
            }
            rev=rev*10+digit;

        }
        return rev;
        
    }
}
